> Helm of Telepathy

Or if you want to #twoweapon, toss the "oLS for an "oR and dump the SoR.  
And if you need Stealth, dump the CoP for an elven cloak.  You can
enchant it higher, so the AC ends up being the same, but you get the
intrinsic.  And personally, I'd rather take an "oMB (or "oESP if you
can't find a HoB) than the "oLS.  But all this is just personal choice.
:)

> Spellcasting outfit:
> Wooden shield (barely hinders spellcasting for V in my experience)
> Gauntlets of dexterity
> SDSM
> AoLS
> Robe
> Helm of Brilliance
> Eye of the Aethiopica (carried, not worn)

> If you haven't got the eye of the aethiopica or some other artifact that 
> confers magic resistance, it's tough to get MR, reflection, AoLS and still 
> cast spells.  If it's late in the game and there are lots of artifacts in 
> existence you might be out of luck.  Of course you could get an amulet of 
> reflection and GDSM and live on the edge...

Quest artifact as source of MR?  Bad.  That's killed one of my monks
before.  

Instead, go with GDSM and an "oR for non-wizards.  Non-wizards, IMO,
absolutely need the Robe, so that's required.  Since we can't use a
CoMR, we need the GDSM.  Reflection then has to come from an "oR.
Wizards, of course, don't need the Robe, so they can go with a CoMR and
SDSM and free up the amulet slot.

In a couple of these schemes, you lose the "oLS for a "oR, but that's
the price you pay for #twoweaponing or having a reliable source of MR.
If it really bothers you, go without Reflection.  It's not really
essential if you have disintegration resistance and fooproofed armor.

